---
import "../styles/global.css";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy - Striff" description="Striff Cookie Policy" canonical="https://striff.io/cookies">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="mb-8 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Cookie Policy</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
      <p class="text-slate-600">Last updated: October 2, 2026</p>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What Are Cookies?</h2>
        <p>Cookies are small text files that are stored on your device when you visit a website. They help the website remember information about your visit, which can make it easier to visit the site again and make the site more useful to you.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">How We Use Cookies</h2>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold">Essential Cookies</h3>
        <p>These cookies are set only when you sign in to the dashboard, and the dashboard cannot work without them:</p>
        <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
          <li><strong><code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">gh_token</code></strong>: keeps you signed in. It holds your GitHub sign-in token, is HTTP-only and secure so page scripts cannot read it, and lasts as long as GitHub keeps that token valid (eight hours) or until you sign out.</li>
          <li><strong><code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">gh_refresh</code></strong>: renews your GitHub sign-in token when it runs out, so you are not asked to sign in again every few hours. It is HTTP-only and secure, and lasts as long as GitHub keeps it valid (about six months, counted again each time it is used) or until you sign out.</li>
          <li><strong><code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">gh_signed_out</code></strong>: set when you sign out, so your next sign-in asks which GitHub account to use. It holds no personal data and lasts one day or until you sign in.</li>
          <li><strong><code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">gh_oauth_state</code></strong>: protects sign-in against forged requests. It lasts 10 minutes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">The dashboard also keeps two small values in your browser's own storage, not in cookies: the repository you last opened, so it opens there next time, and the time of your last sign-in prompt, so it does not prompt you twice in a row. Neither leaves your browser.</p>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold">Analytics Cookies</h3>
        <p>We use PostHog to collect analytics data about how visitors use our website. These cookies help us:</p>
        <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
          <li>See which pages are most popular</li>
          <li>Understand how users navigate through our site</li>
          <li>Identify which content is most engaging</li>
          <li>Improve the overall user experience</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Third-Party Cookies</h2>
        <p>We use PostHog as our analytics provider. PostHog may set cookies on your device to collect analytics information. For more details, please see PostHog's privacy policy.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Types of Data Collected</h2>
        <p>Through cookies, we collect:</p>
        <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
          <li>Browser type and version</li>
          <li>Operating system</li>
          <li>Referring website</li>
          <li>Pages visited and time spent on each page</li>
          <li>Clicks and interactions with page elements</li>
          <li>Approximate geographic location</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Managing Cookies</h2>
        <p>You have several options to manage cookies:</p>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold">Browser Settings</h3>
        <p>Most web browsers allow you to:</p>
        <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
          <li>View what cookies are stored</li>
          <li>Delete individual cookies</li>
          <li>Block all cookies from being set</li>
          <li>Block third-party cookies</li>
          <li>Clear cookies when you close your browser</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold">Browser-Specific Instructions</h3>
        <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
          <li><strong>Chrome:</strong> Settings → Privacy and security → Cookies and other site data</li>
          <li><strong>Firefox:</strong> Settings → Privacy & Security → Cookies and Site Data</li>
          <li><strong>Safari:</strong> Settings → Privacy → Manage Website Data</li>
          <li><strong>Edge:</strong> Settings → Cookies and site permissions → Manage cookies</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What Happens If I Disable Cookies?</h2>
        <p>If you choose to disable cookies:</p>
        <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
          <li>The website will still function normally for viewing content</li>
          <li>You will not be able to sign in to the dashboard</li>
          <li>We will not be able to collect analytics data about your visit</li>
          <li>This may affect our ability to improve the website based on user behavior</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Updates to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this cookie policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Contact Us</h2>
        <p>For questions about our use of cookies, please email us at <a href="mailto:hi@haditechnology.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700">hi@haditechnology.com</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
